-- examples/checks/demand-question-budget.rofl — demand_question_budget: A QUESTION
-- RUNS UNDER ITS OWN BUDGET, counted from nothing, and puts the world's steps back
-- after (f_a_question_spent_the_world_budget). qb_p leaves Y open, so it is
-- answered on demand, and each whynot below unfolds it. Under the world's budget
-- (check_opt) one whynot fits beside the evaluation and eighty in a row do not:
-- a question that spent the world's steps left the later ones (in key order, qb_p(9, 9) last) a wall.
edb(qb_s).
qb_s(0). qb_s(1). qb_s(2). qb_s(3).
qb_o(X, Y) :- qb_s(X), X > 0.
qb_p(X, Y) :- qb_o(X, Y), qb_s(X).
qb_r(X) :- qb_s(X), qb_p(X, 7).
explain_request(whynot, qb_p(0, 9)).
explain_request(whynot, qb_p(1, 9)).
explain_request(whynot, qb_p(2, 9)).
explain_request(whynot, qb_p(3, 9)).
